@subsection refnindex.h

@defun addToRefnIndex (RefnIndex* index, CString refn, CString key) @arrow{} bool
Adds the REFN @code{refn} present in the record having key @code{key} into 
the RefnIndex @code{index}.
@end defun

@defun searchRefnIndex (RefnIndex* index, CString refn) @arrow{} CString
Searches RefnIndex @code{index} for REFN @code{refn}.  If found, it
returns its key, otherwise it returns null.
@end defun

@subsection refns.h

@defun resolveRefnLinks (GNode* node, Database* database) @arrow{} int
Attempt to resolve the REFN links within node.  When successful,
replaces <something> with @@something-else@@.  Returns the number of
unresolved REFN links.
@end defun

@defun addRefn (CString refn, CString key, Database* database) @arrow{} bool
If refn is already present in the refn index,
 if it maps to key, returns true
 if it maps to a different key, returns false
 otherwise, add the mapping refn --> key to the index,
 and return true.
@end defun

@defun removeRefn (CString refn, CString key, Database* database) @arrow{} bool
Searches the refn index within the database, if not found or it maps
to a different key, then returns false.  Otherwise, removes it and
returns true.
@end defun

@defun getRefn (CString refn, Database* database) @arrow{} CString
Searches the index for a mapping for @code{refn}, if found, returns it.
If not found, @code{null} is returned.  */
@end defun

@defun indexByRefn (GNode* node, Database* database) @arrow{} bool
Scans all immediate children of node for REFNs.
For each one found, we add a mapping in the REFN index.

If any already exist with a different key, false (failure) is
returned indicating one or more failures; otherwise true (success)
is returned.  All that do not currently exist are added.

NOTE: needs a better name!
@end defun

@defun annotateWithSupplemental (GNode* node, bool rfmt, Database* database) @arrow{} void

@b{QUESTION:}  Should it copy the tree?
@end defun

@section Internal Functions

@defun createRefnIndexEl (CString refn, CString key) @arrow{} RefnIndexEl*
Creates a new reference index entry.

A @code{RefnIndexEl} is a structure containing the @code{refn} and the
@code{key}.  One is created by @code{addRefnToIndex}.  Applications
should never need to call this function directly.
@end defun

@defun createRefnIndex (void) @arrow{} RefnIndex*
Creates a RefnIndex.

Called by @code{getReferenceIndex}.  Generally applications do not
need to call this directly.
@end defun

@defun deleteRefnIndex (RefnIndex*) @arrow{} void
Deletes a RefnIndex.

Called by @code{deleteDatabase}.  Generally applications do not need
to call this directly.
@end defun

@defun getReferenceIndex (RecordIndex* index, CString fname, IntegerTable* keymap, ErrorLog* elog) @arrow{}  RefnIndex*
Creates a reference index from the records in a Database.  It checks
that REFN values are defined once.

Called by @code{createDatabase} as part of creating a database and
populates it with @code{REFN} values found in the @code{index}.

Generally applications do not need to call this directly.
@end defun

@subsection database.h / database.c

@deftypevar Database* currentDatabase
The current database.

It is intended that eventually the Lifelines port to DeadEnds will
support multiple concurrent databases.

At any time there might be multiple in memory, but one will be the
default for use when a database is not otherwise explicitly specified.
@end deftypevar

