@subsection recordindex.h

@defun addToRecordIndex (RecordIndex*, GNode* root) @arrow{} void
Adds a GNode record tree to a RecordIndex.
@end defun

@defun addrefRecord (GNode* element) @arrow{} void
Increment the reference count of a GNode.
@end defun

@defun releaseRecord (GNode* element) @arrow{} void
Decrement the reference count of a GNode.
If it reaches zero, we do NOT free it.
If it is zero before we decrement, we ABORT.
@end defun

@defun createRecordIndex (void) @arrow{} RecordIndex*
Creates a RecordIndex. The delete function is null to prevent the
trees themselves from being deleted.

Called by @code{createDatabase}.  Normally applications do not need to
call this directly.
@end defun

@defun deleteRecordIndex (RecordIndex*) @arrow{} void
Deletes a RecordIndex.

Called by @code{deleteDatabase}.  Normally applications do not need to
call this directly.
@end defun

@defun searchRecordIndex (RecordIndex*, CString) @arrow{} GNode*
Searches a RecordIndex by key and returns the associated GNode tree.
@end defun

@defmac FORRECORDINDEX (table, gnode, type)
@defmacx ENDRECORDINDEX
Iterates a RecordIndex @code{table} returning only GNode*s
@code{gnode} of a specific type @code{type}.

These come as a pair.  The iteration starts with the
@code{FORRECORDINDEX} and ends with the @code{ENDRECORDINDEX}.
@end defmac
